        { "id": "prt_04d", "sessionID": "ses_104", "messageID": "msg_04", "type": "text", "text": "Not quite - JavaScript runs on a single thread. `db.getPostCount(uid)` returns a `Promise` immediately, not the actual count, so without `await` you'd be handing `res.render` an unresolved promise instead of a number. I added `await` (and marked the function `async` so `await` is allowed) so it waits for the query to finish before rendering." },
        { "id": "prt_04e", "sessionID": "ses_104", "messageID": "msg_04", "type": "step-finish", "reason": "stop", "cost": 0.02, "tokens": { "input": 1600, "output": 380, "reasoning": 0, "cache": { "read": 0, "write": 0 } } }
